# Market/status capture request marker (Phase 5, ADR-038).
#
# `.github/workflows/market-capture.yml` triggers on a push that changes THIS file, so a
# capture is always a deliberate act rather than a side effect of touching market code.
# Bump `revision` (and say why) to ask a runner for another point-in-time capture.
#
# Why a runner at all: the development sandbox sits behind an egress policy that answers
# 403 to CONNECT for api.myfantasyleague.com and api.sleeper.app (ADR-009). A GitHub runner
# has open egress and is the environment the Phase-7 production workflow will run in, so
# evidence gathered there describes the environment that actually matters.

revision: 2
season: 2026
cohorts: study
reason: >-
  First Phase-5 capture. Retains every candidate cohort so the ADR-012 amendment's cohort
  re-measurement can run offline against retained evidence, and takes the first Sleeper
  current-status capture for the player-status artifact.

  Revision 2 re-runs it after revision 1 proved the source path works and then exited 1:
  IS_PPR=0&FCOUNT=14 returned zero rows, which the adapter reported as a critical source
  failure. For a candidate cohort in a measurement that is the finding, not an outage, so
  per-cohort emptiness is now a warning and only an empty capture is critical.
